<body>

<header>
  <h1>Why is the Sky Blue? <span class="zh">| 为什么天空是蓝色的？</span></h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Bilingual explanation across three complexity levels · 三种难度的双语解释</p>
</header>

<nav class="nav-dots" id="navDots">
  <a href="#toddler">👶 Toddler 幼儿</a>
  <a href="#highschool">🎓 High School 高中</a>
  <a href="#phd">🔬 PhD 博士</a>
</nav>

<main>
  <div class="sections-wrapper">

    <!-- ═══════ Toddler ═══════ -->
    <div class="section-card" id="toddler">
      <div class="lang-col en">
        <div class="emoji-head">👶</div>
        <div class="audience-label">For a 3-Year-Old Toddler</div>
        <div class="content">
          <p>When you look up, the sky looks <strong>blue</strong> because sunlight is actually made of <em>all</em> the colors of the rainbow mixed together — red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple!</p>
          <p>When that sunlight travels through the air around Earth, tiny bits of air bump into the light and scatter the <strong>blue</strong> color all over the sky. Blue bounces around more than the other colors, so when you look up, your eyes see lots and lots of blue! 🌈✨</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lang-col zh">
        <div class="emoji-head">👶</div>
        <div class="audience-label">给三岁幼儿</div>
        <div class="content">
          <p>当你抬头看的时候，天空看起来是<strong>蓝色</strong>的，因为阳光实际上是由<em>所有</em>彩虹的颜色混合而成的——红色、橙色、黄色、绿色、蓝色和紫色！</p>
          <p>当阳光穿过地球周围的大气层时，空气中微小的颗粒碰到光线，把<strong>蓝色</strong>散射到整个天空中。蓝色比其他颜色弹来弹去得更多，所以当你抬头看的时候，你的眼睛看到了非常多的蓝色！🌈✨</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════ High School ═══════ -->
    <div class="section-card" id="highschool">
      <div class="lang-col en">
        <div class="emoji-head">🎓</div>
        <div class="audience-label">For a High School Teenager</div>
        <div class="content">
          <p>The sky is blue because of a phenomenon called <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>. Sunlight may look white, but it's actually a mixture of all visible wavelengths — from red (long wavelength, ~700 nm) to violet (short wavelength, ~400 nm).</p>
          <p>As sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it collides with gas molecules (mostly nitrogen and oxygen) that are much smaller than the wavelength of visible light.</p>
          <p>These collisions cause the light to scatter. Crucially, the amount of scattering is <strong>inversely proportional to the fourth power of the wavelength</strong> (scattering ∝ 1/λ⁴). This means shorter wavelengths (blue and violet) are scattered roughly <strong>10 times more strongly</strong> than longer wavelengths (red and orange).</p>
          <p>But wait — if violet scatters even more than blue, why isn't the sky violet? Two reasons:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>The Sun emits more light at blue wavelengths than violet.</li>
            <li>The human eye is much more sensitive to blue than violet.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>The combination of these factors means the sky appears <strong>blue</strong> to us. At sunrise or sunset, sunlight travels through more atmosphere, scattering the blue light away and letting the reds and oranges through — which is why sunsets are red.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lang-col zh">
        <div class="emoji-head">🎓</div>
        <div class="audience-label">给高中生</div>
        <div class="content">
          <p>天空是蓝色的，这是因为一种叫做<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的现象。阳光看起来是白色的，但实际上它是所有可见波长的混合——从红色（长波长，约 700 纳米）到紫色（短波长，约 400 纳米）。</p>
          <p>当阳光进入地球大气层时，它会与比可见光波长小得多的气体分子（主要是氮气和氧气）发生碰撞。</p>
          <p>这些碰撞导致光线发生散射。关键的是，散射的量与波长的<strong>四次方成反比</strong>（散射 ∝ 1/λ⁴）。这意味着较短的波长（蓝色和紫色）比较长的波长（红色和橙色）<strong>散射大约强 10 倍</strong>。</p>
          <p>但等等——如果紫色比蓝色散射得更强，为什么天空不是紫色的？原因有二：</p>
          <ol>
            <li>太阳在蓝光波长处的辐射比紫光波长处更强。</li>
            <li>人眼对蓝色的敏感度远高于紫色。</li>
          </ol>
          <p>这些因素的组合使得天空在我们眼中呈现出<strong>蓝色</strong>。在日出或日落时，阳光需要穿过更厚的大气层，蓝光被散射掉，而红色和橙色则得以穿透——这就是为什么日落是红色的。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════ PhD ═══════ -->
    <div class="section-card" id="phd">
      <div class="lang-col en">
        <div class="emoji-head">🔬</div>
        <div class="audience-label">For a Physics PhD</div>
        <div class="content">
          <p>The blue sky is a classic demonstration of <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>, arising from elastic scattering of electromagnetic radiation by particles much smaller than the incident wavelength (d ≪ λ).</p>

          <p><strong>Microscopic Derivation:</strong> Treating atmospheric molecules (N₂, O₂) as induced electric dipoles, an incident plane wave polarizes each molecule, inducing a dipole moment p = αE₀, where α is the molecular polarizability.</p>

          <p class="eq">dI/dΩ = (k⁴|α|² / 16π²ε₀²r²) · I₀ · sin²θ</p>

          <p>Integrating over solid angle gives the total cross section:</p>

          <p class="eq">σ ∝ 1/λ⁴</p>

          <p>This 1/λ⁴ dependence is the hallmark of Rayleigh scattering. For dry air at STP, n ≈ 1.000293 and n₀ ≈ 2.55 × 10²⁵ m⁻³, yielding an extinction coefficient that correctly predicts the observed attenuation of direct sunlight.</p>

          <p><strong>Spectral &amp; Biological Considerations:</strong> The solar spectrum at the top of the atmosphere approximates a blackbody at T ≈ 5778 K. The scattered radiance spectrum L(λ) ∝ (1/λ⁴)Bλ(5778 K) is therefore blue-shifted relative to the solar spectrum.</p>

          <p>Color perception enters through the <strong>CIE 1931 color matching functions</strong> x̄(λ), ȳ(λ), z̄(λ). Despite λ ≈ 400 nm scattering more strongly, the perceived color is saturated blue (not violet) because:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>The solar spectral irradiance drops significantly in the near-UV/violet (Planck distribution).</li>
            <li>The CIE z̄(λ) function (violet response) has much lower magnitude than x̄(λ) and ȳ(λ) in the 400–450 nm band.</li>
            <li>Multiple scattering and aerosol (Mie) contributions add a whitening component that shifts the perceived hue.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>A full treatment would also account for atmospheric aerosol loading (Ångström exponent), molecular anisotropy (King correction factor), and altitude dependence of column density along the line of sight.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lang-col zh">
        <div class="emoji-head">🔬</div>
        <div class="audience-label">给物理学博士</div>
        <div class="content">
          <p>蓝色天空是<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的一个经典例证，它源于电磁辐射被远小于入射波长的粒子（d ≪ λ）所弹性散射。</p>

          <p><strong>微观推导：</strong>将大气分子（N₂、O₂）视为感应电偶极子，入射平面波使每个分子极化，产生偶极矩 p = αE₀，其中 α 是分子极化率。</p>

          <p class="eq">dI/dΩ = (k⁴|α|² / 16π²ε₀²r²) · I₀ · sin²θ</p>

          <p>对立体角积分得到总截面：</p>

          <p class="eq">σ ∝ 1/λ⁴</p>

          <p>这种 1/λ⁴ 依赖性正是瑞利散射的特征。对于标准温度和压力（STP）下的干燥空气，折射率 n ≈ 1.000293，分子数密度为 n₀ ≈ 2.55 × 10²⁵ m⁻³，所得消光系数能够正确预测观测到的直射阳光衰减。</p>

          <p><strong>光谱与生物学考虑：</strong>大气顶部的太阳光谱近似为一个黑体谱，温度 T ≈ 5778 K。因此，散射辐射谱 L(λ) ∝ (1/λ⁴)Bλ(5778 K) 相对于太阳光谱发生了蓝移。</p>

          <p>颜色感知通过 <strong>CIE 1931 颜色匹配函数</strong> x̄(λ)、ȳ(λ)、z̄(λ) 介入。尽管 λ ≈ 400 nm 的散射更强，但感知颜色为饱和蓝色（非紫色），这是因为：</p>
          <ol>
            <li>太阳光谱辐照度在近紫外/紫色区域（普朗克分布）显著下降。</li>
            <li>CIE z̄(λ) 函数（紫色响应）在 400–450 nm 波段的幅值远低于 x̄(λ) 和 ȳ(λ)。</li>
            <li>多重散射和气溶胶（米氏散射）贡献添加了使感知色调偏移的白化成分。</li>
          </ol>
          <p>一个完整的处理还应考虑大气气溶胶负荷（Ångström 指数）、分子各向异性（King 修正因子），以及沿视线方向的柱密度随高度的依赖性。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</main>

<footer>
  Why is the Sky Blue? · 为什么天空是蓝色的？
  &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; Bilingual Slide Deck
</footer>

<script>
  // ── Scroll reveal ──
  const cards = document.querySelectorAll('.section-card');
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(entry => {
      if (entry.isIntersecting) {
        entry.target.classList.add('visible');
      }
    });
  }, { threshold: 0.1 });
  cards.forEach(c => observer.observe(c));

  // ── Active nav dot on scroll ──
  const sections = document.querySelectorAll('.section-card');
  const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.nav-dots a');

  const navObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(entry => {
      if (entry.isIntersecting) {
        const id = entry.target.id;
        navLinks.forEach(link => {
          link.classList.toggle('active', link.getAttribute('href') === '#' + id);
        });
      }
    });
  }, { threshold: 0.3 });
  sections.forEach(s => navObserver.observe(s));
</script>
</body>
</html>
"}

